{"headword":"מַשָּׂא⁴","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Isaiah 14:28\" href=\"/Isaiah.14.28\">Is 14:28</a></sup> <strong>utterance, oracle (</strong>cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, נָשָׂא\" href=\"/BDB,_נָשָׂא\", dir=\"rtl\">נשׂא</a> <strong>1 b</strong> (6); Gf <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:33\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.33\">Je 23:33</a><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 14:28\" href=\"/Isaiah.14.28\">Is 14:28</a> +; usually cstr. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.1\">13:1</a> +;—of prophetic <em>utterance:</em> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:25\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.25\">2 K 9:25</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 14:28\" href=\"/Isaiah.14.28\">Is 14:28</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 12:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.12.10\">Ez 12:10</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 24:27\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.24.27\">2 Ch 24:27</a> (c. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ בָבֶל</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.1\">Is 13:1</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ מוֹאָב</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 15:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.15.1\">15:1</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 17:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.17.1\">17:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 19:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.19.1\">19:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 21:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.21.1\">21:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 21:11\" href=\"/Isaiah.21.11\">11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 22:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.22.1\">22:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 23:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.23.1\">23:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 30:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.30.6\">30:6</a> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 1:1\" href=\"/Nahum.1.1\">Na 1:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ בערב</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 21:13\" href=\"/Isaiah.21.13\">Is 21:13</a> is later ins. (Di); <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> = <em>revelation</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמּ׳ אֲשֶׁר חָזָה חֲבַקּוּק הַנָּבִיא</span> <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 1:1\" href=\"/Habakkuk.1.1\">Hb 1:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ י׳</span> <em>utterance of</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:33\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.33\">Je 23:33</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:34\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.34\">34</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:36\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.36\">36</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:38\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.38\">38</a><sup>(×3)</sup> (cf. <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:25\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.25\">2 K 9:25</a>), vid. also v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:33\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.33\">33b</a> (read <span dir=\"rtl\">אַתֶּם הַמַּשָּׂא</span>), with word-play,—sq. <span dir=\"rtl\">וְנָטַשְׁתִּי</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:36\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.36\">36b</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ דְבַר י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.1\">Zc 9:1</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">בארץ</span>), <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 12:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.12.1\">12:1</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל־יִשְׂרָאֵל</span>), <a data-ref=\"Malachi 1:1\" href=\"/Malachi.1.1\">Mal 1:1</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶל־יִשׂ׳</span>).—<a data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:1\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.1\">Pr 31:1</a> v. i. <a data-ref=\"BDB, מַשָּׂא\" href=\"/BDB,_מַשָּׂא\", dir=\"rtl\">מַשָּׂא</a>, p. 601 supr.; in <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:1\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.1\">30:1</a> read <span dir=\"rtl\">מִמַּשָּׂא</span> <em>from Massa</em> (Mühlau, De), or <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמַּשָּׂאִי</span> (Wild), which however is perhaps not original, but borrowed from <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:1\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.1\">31:1</a> (cf. Wild<sup>ad loc.</sup> Frankenberg<sup>Spr. p. 5</sup>; corrupt name of Agur’s home or tribe, Kau)."}]},"rid":"BDB06539","strong_numbers":["4853"],"next_hw":"מַשֹּא","prev_hw":"מַשָּׂא³","all_cited":true,"ordinal":"III.","quotes":[],"GK":["5362"],"TWOT":["1421d","1421e"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. Wit